Hi Matt
I'm currently working on setting up FC4 and Bluetooth. I have made lots of
progress by searching on the web, and I have read lots of web pages.
Currently, I have managed to create a PAN profile with a FC4 box and a
Windows XP one. I have follow the instructions in
http://www.jeremythompson.uklinux.net/RH8-0/bluezhowto.pdf
http://bluez.sourceforge.net/contrib/HOWTO-PAN

Moreover, this web page is related with Palm and Linux 
http://www.harbaum.org/till/palm/bluetooth/

I don't know what is your degree of experience (I'm really new with Bluez),
so perhaps you know this, but you have to change hci.conf file also to
accommodate to your devices. 

Feel free to write again if you have some specific question, I will try to
help you if I know how...

Esther

PS. Do you know something about sdpd? Yesterday I wrote an email and nobody
replies, I get an error, and can't discover added services in my linux box
from other devices :(

